WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.153
- [Interviewer] So Tina,
where are you from?

00:00:06.153 --> 00:00:08.900
- I'm originally from Portland, Oregon.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.400
- [Interviewer] Portland, how
long have you been down here?

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.471
- Since '97.

00:00:11.471 --> 00:00:14.310
- [Interviewer] You've
been on skid row since '97.

00:00:14.310 --> 00:00:16.870
- No I've been in Los Angeles since '97.

00:00:16.870 --> 00:00:18.933
- [Interviewer] Oh and how'd
you end up on skid row?

00:00:19.830 --> 00:00:22.097
- I was married to a guy that,

00:00:22.097 --> 00:00:26.088
the marriage didn't go
to well between us two.

00:00:26.088 --> 00:00:29.759
- [Interviewer] That'll happen.

00:00:29.759 --> 00:00:30.842
It'll happen.

00:00:32.130 --> 00:00:33.490
And you're sleeping where?

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:34.970
- I started in Los Angeles.

00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:37.700
The old side of the old women's center.

00:00:37.700 --> 00:00:38.730
- [Interviewer] The what women's center?

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:42.044
- The old side of the old
downtown women's center.

00:00:42.044 --> 00:00:43.240
- [Interviewer] And that's
a nice place to sleep?

00:00:43.240 --> 00:00:45.830
- Yep I have my own apartment.

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:49.490
I have my own refrigerator,
but we share, I have to share,

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.960
we have a community bathroom
and a community kitchen.

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:55.110
- [Interviewer] Yeah but it's
a nice warm place to sleep.

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:55.943
- Oh yeah.

00:00:55.943 --> 00:00:57.063
- [Interviewer] Beats the street.

00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:00.143
Have you been on the streets as well?

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.293
- Before I moved in here.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:05.043
- [Interviewer] Yeah that's rough.

00:01:05.043 --> 00:01:06.680
I've been down here.

00:01:06.680 --> 00:01:08.302
Some nights where it's so cold

00:01:08.302 --> 00:01:10.560
and people are just laying

00:01:10.560 --> 00:01:11.800
on the sidewalk all night.

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:14.820
It's like, oh, and then
when it rains or whatever,

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:17.505
it's like, it's just so rough.

00:01:17.505 --> 00:01:18.338
- I know.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:21.990
- [Interviewer] What's the
craziest thing you've seen

00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:23.210
down here in skid row?

00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:26.360
I've seen crazy stuff, but
you're living down here.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:27.910
So you've seen it.

00:01:27.910 --> 00:01:29.293
- I've seen it all.

00:01:33.383 --> 00:01:35.610
- [Interviewer] Tell me a story or two.

00:01:35.610 --> 00:01:37.290
- I've seen women,

00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:38.123
let me see,

00:01:38.123 --> 00:01:41.553
I've seen women run down the street naked.

00:01:41.553 --> 00:01:46.000
God, totally crazy.

00:01:46.000 --> 00:01:47.800
- [Interviewer] I saw a woman one morning,

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:48.900
sun was just coming up,

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:51.460
I saw a woman taking a crap in the middle

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:54.330
of a big crowded sidewalk.

00:01:54.330 --> 00:01:56.405
It's just like, she
just dropped her pants.

00:01:56.405 --> 00:01:58.793
Took a dump right there on the sidewalk.

00:02:00.520 --> 00:02:01.740
Right in the broad daylight.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.573
It was crazy.

00:02:04.254 --> 00:02:05.383
I haven't seen that before.

00:02:08.490 --> 00:02:10.285
So your nose, what happened to your nose?

00:02:10.285 --> 00:02:12.000
- I got hit with a pipe wrench.

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:14.700
- [Interviewer] You got
hit with a pipe wrench?

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:16.000
That was here on skid row?

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.113
Yeah it's a rough neighborhood, isn't it?

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:29.780
Yeah that'll wreck your day, right?

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:30.830
- [Tina] Yeah it did.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:34.930
- [Interviewer] And you
never got it straightened out

00:02:34.930 --> 00:02:35.913
or anything?

00:02:37.076 --> 00:02:38.076
You just left it be.

00:02:40.580 --> 00:02:41.670
Isn't there a place somewhere down here

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.804
you can get that taken care?

00:02:42.804 --> 00:02:45.290
- I'm not, I'm not going
to get it taken care of.

00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:49.767
- [Interviewer] I like your pants.

00:02:49.767 --> 00:02:51.240
- [Tina] Oh thanks.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:52.876
- [Interviewer] Let me see your shoes too.

00:02:52.876 --> 00:02:55.817
Look at those things, very fun.

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:58.173
So do you have family?

00:02:58.173 --> 00:02:59.060
Do you have kids?

00:02:59.060 --> 00:02:59.893
Do you have anything like?

00:02:59.893 --> 00:03:02.633
- I've got a 21 year old
daughter, three grandkids.

00:03:04.420 --> 00:03:07.260
My dad got remarried
after my mom passed away

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.963
and I've got two older
sisters, one younger brother.

00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.263
My stepsister and two stepbrothers.

00:03:19.590 --> 00:03:22.100
Nieces and nephews like crazy.

00:03:22.100 --> 00:03:23.966
- [Interviewer] Yeah
they're all in Portland?

00:03:23.966 --> 00:03:25.467
- [Tina] All up in Oregon, yup.

00:03:25.467 --> 00:03:26.790
- [Interviewer] And do
they know you're down here?

00:03:26.790 --> 00:03:27.623
- [Tina] Yup.

00:03:28.710 --> 00:03:30.790
- [Interviewer] Do you,
do you talk to them?

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:31.623
- [Tina] Oh yeah.

00:03:31.623 --> 00:03:32.960
- [Interviewer] Yeah.

00:03:32.960 --> 00:03:35.633
So you're doing drugs at all
or no, you seem really clean.

00:03:35.633 --> 00:03:36.466
- [Tina] No.

00:03:36.466 --> 00:03:37.299
- [Interviewer] You seem clean.

00:03:37.299 --> 00:03:39.883
- [Tina] Yeah I've always,
I've been clean for years.

00:03:40.899 --> 00:03:41.732
- [Interviewer] You just can't get it,

00:03:41.732 --> 00:03:45.267
you just can't get money
together to get a job or do--

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:48.410
- [Tina] No, no, I'm
on, I'm on disability.

00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:49.660
- [Interviewer] For what?

00:03:49.660 --> 00:03:50.910
- [Tina] My seizures.

00:03:50.910 --> 00:03:51.743
- [Interviewer] Oh, you have seizures?

00:03:51.743 --> 00:03:53.180
- [Tina] Yeah I use to, I don't have,

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.640
I haven't had them in years.

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.430
- [Interviewer] Like grand mal seizures?

00:03:56.430 --> 00:03:58.120
Yeah, oof.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.843
And those are brought out just by what?

00:04:00.843 --> 00:04:04.412
- [Tina] Just everything,
stress, there's different things.

00:04:04.412 --> 00:04:05.753
- [Interviewer] Oh man.

00:04:05.753 --> 00:04:08.223
Yeah that'll that'll slow you down,

00:04:11.820 --> 00:04:12.810
but what, what,

00:04:12.810 --> 00:04:13.643
what are your dreams?

00:04:13.643 --> 00:04:14.476
What would you love to see happen

00:04:14.476 --> 00:04:15.710
in the next five years in your life?

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.060
Where would you like to be?

00:04:19.060 --> 00:04:20.073
- Married again.

00:04:29.291 --> 00:04:30.124
- [Interviewer] Do you
talk to your daughter?

00:04:30.124 --> 00:04:31.533
- Oh yeah I talk to her a lot.

00:04:33.650 --> 00:04:36.340
- [Interviewer] She's got a
family, or she's working or--

00:04:36.340 --> 00:04:38.660
- She's in school right now.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:40.423
She's got one more year of college.

00:04:42.990 --> 00:04:44.058
- [Interviewer] That's good,
where's she going to school?

00:04:44.058 --> 00:04:46.558
- Portland State University.

00:04:46.558 --> 00:04:48.975
- [Interviewer] Oh excellent.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.260
Well can I give you a little something to

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.280
make your day a little easier?

00:04:56.280 --> 00:04:57.450
- Yeah.

00:04:57.450 --> 00:04:58.460
- [Interviewer] Excellent.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:05:03.083
So are you making money
here on the street?

00:05:04.019 --> 00:05:06.280
- Not as much as I used to

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:07.597
- [Interviewer] But there
there'll be guys that pick you up.

00:05:07.597 --> 00:05:08.440
- Yeah.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:09.460
- [Interviewer] And how
often does that go on?

00:05:09.460 --> 00:05:10.580
- Every night.

00:05:10.580 --> 00:05:12.040
- [Interviewer] Every night.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.120
So what hours is that going on?

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.610
- All depends how my night goes.

00:05:15.610 --> 00:05:18.130
I'm in culinary school right now.

00:05:18.130 --> 00:05:21.330
So I know I only out, I come
out here once in a while.

00:05:21.330 --> 00:05:22.163
- [Interviewer] Oh really?

00:05:22.163 --> 00:05:22.996
- Yeah.

00:05:22.996 --> 00:05:24.180
- [Interviewer] You're
going to culinary school?

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:25.403
Good for you.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:30.270
And do you do business with these guys?

00:05:30.270 --> 00:05:31.590
You do it in their car or
they take you somewhere--

00:05:31.590 --> 00:05:33.740
- No, hotel, cars,

00:05:33.740 --> 00:05:35.064
- [Interviewer] Wherever?

00:05:35.064 --> 00:05:37.181
And how much money will you make?

00:05:37.181 --> 00:05:39.030
- On a really good
night, over 200 dollars,

00:05:39.030 --> 00:05:39.990
on a really good night.

00:05:39.990 --> 00:05:42.990
- [Interviewer] Really, that's good.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.763
- Of course my dude's in jail.

00:05:49.690 --> 00:05:50.660
- [Interviewer] Who's that?

00:05:50.660 --> 00:05:51.620
- His name is Casey.

00:05:51.620 --> 00:05:52.453
He's in jail.

00:05:52.453 --> 00:05:54.520
They busted him for sales.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:56.303
He didn't wasn't selling anything.

00:05:57.440 --> 00:06:00.699
What it was, they pulled
up on his homeboy,

00:06:00.699 --> 00:06:02.723
and his homeboys girl.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:07.110
Well they pulled him out
the indication with him

00:06:07.110 --> 00:06:09.103
and three females snitched on him.

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:12.690
So he's in jail.

00:06:12.690 --> 00:06:15.880
He was suppose to get out in
January but a riot broke out.

00:06:15.880 --> 00:06:18.713
So he won't be getting out
until October of this year.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.150
- [Interviewer] Where can I drop you off?

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:28.170
I'm going to take you somewhere.

00:06:28.170 --> 00:06:30.705
- Seventh and Town on the
other side of the light.

00:06:30.705 --> 00:06:31.690
- [Interviewer] Okay.

00:06:31.690 --> 00:06:32.843
You going to go around the block here?

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:37.953
- I got shot.

00:06:37.953 --> 00:06:38.786
- [Interviewer] You got shot?

00:06:38.786 --> 00:06:42.340
- Yeah down Agatha and Crocker.

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:44.560
Three times, I got two bullets in my back,

00:06:44.560 --> 00:06:47.263
they told me, we moved
the one out of my arm.

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:52.020
- [Interviewer] And you still
have bullets in your body?

00:06:52.020 --> 00:06:52.853
- In my back,

00:06:52.853 --> 00:06:55.583
they can't pull them out because
they'll leave me paralyzed.

00:06:57.710 --> 00:06:58.700
I'm a survivor.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:00.620
I've survived down here for years.

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:03.040
- [Interviewer] Yes I've
been seeing you down here

00:07:03.040 --> 00:07:05.551
for about five, six years,

00:07:05.551 --> 00:07:09.540
you actually, you look a little cleaner,

00:07:09.540 --> 00:07:11.340
and better now than I saw you last time.

00:07:11.340 --> 00:07:14.090
I think when I photographed
you the first time it was a

00:07:15.777 --> 00:07:17.253
you didn't look so good.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.680
Well, good luck to you.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:24.284
- Oh yeah.

00:07:24.284 --> 00:07:25.430
- [Interviewer] You seem to be
doing in the right direction

00:07:25.430 --> 00:07:26.263
at least.

